{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1546506-why-the-30s","id":1546506,"title":"Why the 30s?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-11-30T19:30:45-08:00","id":1546506,"title":"Why the 30s?","content":"Haven't had a chance to dive deep into the new edition, just getting back into gaming...but I see that the setting of Adventure! in 2E has been moved up to the 1930s? I was just wondering if there's a developers' reason for why this change? The original game's focus on the 20s was one of the things that first got me researching the Jazz Age in depth, I'm sad to see it go! Is the new setting simply taking place a decade later, after the events of 1E, or is this a complete reboot, with the Hammersmith event now occurring later in time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-30T21:27:50-08:00","id":1546513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1546506-why-the-30s#post1546506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't had a chance to dive deep into the new edition, just getting back into gaming...but I see that the setting of Adventure! in 2E has been moved up to the 1930s? I was just wondering if there's a developers' reason for why this change? The original game's focus on the 20s was one of the things that first got me researching the Jazz Age in depth, I'm sad to see it go! Is the new setting simply taking place a decade later, after the events of 1E, or is this a complete reboot, with the Hammersmith event now occurring later in time?</div> </div> </div> </div>TC: Adventure! is depicted in the 1930s, a decade after the 1920s of the original Adventure! I\u2019m pretty sure the Hammersmith event still takes place in 1922. OOC I think the developers moved it to the 1930s because it\u2019s a more iconic time, being the birthplace of pulp heroes, and also because there are more iconic villains to confront (i.e. Nazis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":25411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","user":"TravisLegge","date":". 12-01-2024, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-30T21:33:56-08:00","id":1546514,"title":"","content":"Moderators: when you approve the post above, please delete the hyphen in \u201cHammersmith.\u201d Right margins that don\u2019t line up drive me crazy and I was trying to fix it, but it didn\u2019t work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-30T23:39:06-08:00","id":1546516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1546506-why-the-30s#post1546506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haven't had a chance to dive deep into the new edition, just getting back into gaming...but I see that the setting of Adventure! in 2E has been moved up to the 1930s? I was just wondering if there's a developers' reason for why this change? The original game's focus on the 20s was one of the things that first got me researching the Jazz Age in depth, I'm sad to see it go! Is the new setting simply taking place a decade later, after the events of 1E, or is this a complete reboot, with the Hammersmith event now occurring later in time?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's just a timeskip.<br /> <br /> According to TC developer Ian Watson, a large part of the reason for the timeskip was giving PCs the opportunity to punch Nazis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T11:55:20-08:00","id":1546597,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I guess more people are certainly more aware of the 30s onward in entertainment than the 20s...So, to be clear, everything in my 1st Edition book is still canon, setting-wise? 2E just moves the story ahead abit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-04T23:45:00-08:00","id":1546628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1546506-why-the-30s?p=1546597#post1546597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I guess more people are certainly more aware of the 30s onward in entertainment than the 20s...So, to be clear, everything in my 1st Edition book is still canon, setting-wise? 2E just moves the story ahead abit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mainly, though 2E makes it so all three of the super prototypes were at the Hammersmith Incident (Max Mercer (Talent), Michael Donighal (Nova), Sara Kaur, a.k.a. S.K. Bhurano (Psiad)).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-05T01:15:42-08:00","id":1546631,"title":"","content":"Maybe they just prefer the culture of the 1930s. Sound films, jazz has a different sound, Vauderville is being replaced by radio, and the pulps were more dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T18:33:36-07:00","id":1549793,"title":"","content":"In the 1930's the world is still a mystery to many people. Adventures against that backdrop can be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:georgia\">Organizer for the Dead Gamers Society: The So Cal World of Darkness Meetup. </span><a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/85-drumheller","name":"Drumheller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar85_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-08T06:54:14-07:00","id":1550838,"title":"","content":"Figure more people would prefer to play Indiana Jones than Jay Gatsby.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-n